# The scorekeeping half of a small game: single values, players, and rules that apply
# by themselves. Nobody calls the rules; after every change they are applied until
# nothing moves.
#   ./intent build examples/arcade.intent -o build/arcade
#   build/arcade save.log        (the file makes it remember between runs)

The score is a number.
The best starts at 0.
The level starts at 1.
The lives start at 3.
The mood is text that starts at "calm".

Players is a collection where each player has a unique name, points and a rank (text).
Reject duplicates.

Join: add a player.
Hit: increase the score by a given amount.
Miss: decrease the lives by 1.
Restart: set the score to 0, set the lives to 3.
Status: show the score, the best, the level and the lives.
Show the mood.
Award: increase the points of the player with a given name by a given amount.
Leaders: show the top 3 players by points.
Rivals: show the names of players whose points are over the best.

# Standing rules.
When the score is over the best, the best becomes the score.
The level is always 3 if the score is at least 50, otherwise 2 if the score is at least 10, otherwise 1.
When the lives are under 1, the mood becomes "game over".
When the lives are at least 1 and the level is 3, the mood becomes "excited".
When the lives are at least 1 and the level is under 3, the mood becomes "calm".
Whenever a player's points are at least 100, their rank becomes "gold".
As soon as a player's points are under 0, remove them.
